      "source_question_id": "246e924017c48fa1f069361c44133fdf4f0386e1",
      "predicted_answer": "The formula for the **gated sharing cell** (gated sharing cell) described in the provided text is:\n\n**Gate computation:**\n$$ \\mathbf{g}_{\\text{fake}} = \\sigma \\left( \\mathbf{H}_{\\text{shared}} \\mathbf{W}_{\\text{fake}} + \\mathbf{b}_{\\text{fake}} \\right) $$\nwhere $\\sigma$ is the sigmoid function.\n\n**Gated shared features (element-wise multiplication):**\n$$ \\mathbf{H}_{\\text{fake}} = \\mathbf{H}_{\\text{shared}} \\odot \\mathbf{g}_{\\text{fake}} $$\nwhere $\\odot$ denotes element-wise multiplication.\n\n**Formal definition from text (shared layer output):**\n$$ \\mathbf{H}_{\\text{shared}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{1 \\times l(d_p+d_w)} $$\n$$ \\mathbf{W}_{\\text{fake}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{l(d_p+d_w) \\times l(d_p+d_w)}, \\quad \\mathbf{b}_{\\text{fake}} \\in \\mathbb{R}^{1 \\times l(d_p+d_w)} $$\n$$ \\mathbf{g}_{\\text{fake}} = \\sigma \\left( \\mathbf{H}_{\\text{shared}} \\mathbf{W}_{\\text{fake}} + \\mathbf{b}_{\\text{fake}} \\right) $$\n\nThe stance detection task uses an identical gating mechanism with its own parameters $\\mathbf{W}_{\\text{stance}}$ and $\\mathbf{b}_{\\text{stance}}$ to compute $\\mathbf{g}_{\\text{stance}}$ and $\\mathbf{H}_{\\text{stance}} = \\mathbf{H}_{\\text{shared}} \\odot \\mathbf{g}_{\\text{stance}}$.\n\n**Reason for single-gate mechanism (from text):**\n1. The Transformer encoder in the shared layer efficiently captures long-range dependencies, removing the need for complex recurrent gates (LSTM/GRU).\n2. A single-gate mechanism is more convenient for training.",
