    {
      "question_id": "qasper_test_a71fb012631e6a8854d5945b6d0ab2ab8e7b7ee6",
      "source_question_id": "a71fb012631e6a8854d5945b6d0ab2ab8e7b7ee6",
      "predicted_answer": "The paper is **\"F-Score Driven Max-Margin Neural Network for Chinese Named Entity Recognition\"** (Qasper et al., 2016/2017, likely CCL/NLPCC). It introduces a **B-LSTM + Max-Margin Neural Network (MMNN)** with **F-Score Driven Training** for Chinese NER on Sina Weibo data. Key components: (1) B-LSTM baseline with Jieba word segmentation features and word2vec embeddings; (2) MMNN combining B-LSTM with CRF transition scores (max-margin objective); (3) Two F-Score driven models — Model I (F-Score driven training) and Model II (integrated F-Score driven training) — optimizing directly for F1-score; (4) Positional character embeddings with word segmentation features on Jieba-segmented Sina Weibo corpus; (5) Evaluation on Chinese social media NER dataset showing SOTA F1, outperforming B-LSTM+CRF and Peng & Dredze 2016 baselines.",
      "prediction_missing": false,
